.TH "LMM" "1" "Nov 2026" "lmm 2.3.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
lmm-load-order-list - List the effective file load order


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm load-order list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List each of the game's file load orders as lmm would write it, first
loaded first: the archive, what placed it, and the mod that ships it.

.PP
The "placed by" column says why an archive is where it is: order (the
profile's order), default (not in the order yet: its alphabetical place),
or external (not deployed by lmm; it keeps its place in the list).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lmm or ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/lmm or ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--id\fP=""
	the load order (default: the game's only one)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output JSON instead of text; mutating commands print their result, --dry-run prints the plan; never prompts

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="off"
	diagnostic log level written to stderr (off, error, warn, info, debug)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colored output (NO_COLOR env is also honored)

.PP
\fB--no-hooks\fP[=false]
	disable all hooks

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile (default: active profile)

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  lmm load-order list
  lmm load-order list -p coop --json
.EE


